VeridianOS: AlignedSizeAttached: drop the unused lambda parameter

GCC reported unused parameter 'window' [-Wunused-parameter] in the
QQuickItem::windowChanged handler in src/primitives/alignedsizeattached.cpp:22.
The lambda reads the window from m_item->window() (the same object the
signal carries); declare it without the parameter, which Qt's connect()
accepts for a slot taking fewer arguments than the signal. No behaviour
change.

diff -ru a/src/primitives/alignedsizeattached.cpp b/src/primitives/alignedsizeattached.cpp
--- a/src/primitives/alignedsizeattached.cpp	2026-10-08 17:32:51.031542309 -0400
+++ b/src/primitives/alignedsizeattached.cpp	2026-10-08 17:32:51.165275619 -0400
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
         return;
     }
 
-    connect(m_item, &QQuickItem::windowChanged, this, [this](QQuickWindow *window) {
+    connect(m_item, &QQuickItem::windowChanged, this, [this]() {
         if (m_window) {
             m_window->removeEventFilter(this);
         }
